      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityneighborhoods.nyc/sunnyside",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sunnyside’s name comes from a 19th‑century farm owned by the Bragaw family, whose estate offered expansive views of the surrounding hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityneighborhoods.nyc/sunnyside",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the late 19th century, the LIRR operated a short‑lived Sunnyside Station on the “White Line,” competing with the Flushing and North Side Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunnyside_station_(New_York)",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The proposed Sunnyside LIRR station will serve both the LIRR and Metro‑North, giving Penn Station access once the Penn Station Access project finishes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
